<article class="env-lemma" id="0F7Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F7Z">Lemma <span data-tag="0F7Z">15.97.8</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring and let $f \in A$ be a nonzerodivisor. Let $M^\bullet $ be a complex of $f$-torsion free $A$-modules. If $\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d^ i \bmod f^2)$ surjects onto $\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d^ i \bmod f)$, then the canonical map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (1, d^ i) : (\eta _ fM)^ i / f(\eta _ fM)^ i \longrightarrow f^ iM^ i/f^{i + 1}M^ i \oplus f^{i + 1}M^{i + 1}/f^{i + 2}M^{i + 1}  \]
</div>
  <p> identifies the left hand side with a direct sum of submodules of the right hand side. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      With notation as in Remark <a href="/tag/0F7S" data-tag="0F7S">15.97.5</a> we define a map $t^{-1} : Z^ i \to (\eta _ fM)^ i / f(\eta _ fM)^ i$. Namely, for $x \in M^ i$ with $d^ i(x) = f^2y$ we send the class of $x$ in $Z^ i$ to the class of $f^ ix$ in $(\eta _ fM)^ i / f(\eta _ fM)^ i$. We omit the verification that this is well defined; the assumption of the lemma exactly signifies that the domain of this operation is all of $Z^ i$. Then $t \circ t^{-1} = \text{id}_{Z^ i}$. Hence $t^{-1}$ defines a splitting of the short exact sequence in Remark <a href="/tag/0F7S" data-tag="0F7S">15.97.5</a> and the resulting direct sum decomposition 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (\eta _ fM)^ i / f(\eta _ fM)^ i = Z^ i \oplus B^{i + 1}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is compatible with the map displayed in the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>